# Act 3 open world (log4/gen_world.py): side content on the world map's destinations, Age 772-780.
# Flags 409-428 (see gen_world.py). Stone Dragon Balls = BF items 15-21 ("Dragon Ball 1-7", descriptions say stone).
# Take-off lists (fly_*) are generated into act3_world_fly.scene.

# ---------- Orange Star City (17:42, BF 3:4: Orange Star High)
list osc_arrive
if_flag 410 osc_seen
set_flag 410
narrate Orange Star City. Half the skyline is gone. The other half has its windows boarded up.
narrate A school stands at the end of the street. The paint on its sign still says ORANGE STAR HIGH.
say android17 Somebody's still living here. I can hear a radio.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label osc_seen
list osc_school
narrate The front doors are chained shut. A notice, sun-bleached: CLOSED UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE. Age 767.
say android18 Nobody ever made us go to school.
say android17 Lucky us.
stop
list osc_police
narrate Officer: The station's empty. I just... keep showing up. Somebody has to direct traffic, even if there's no traffic.
stop
list osc_girl
narrate Girl: My dad says the androids are just a story to scare kids. My dad also says Hercule is coming to save us.
stop
list osc_hercule
if_flag 411 herc_after
narrate Hercule: H-hold it right there! You're looking at the World Martial Arts Champion! Hercule!
say android17 The champion of what? There haven't been any tournaments in years.
narrate Hercule: The... the title is still valid! Nobody took it from me!
say android18 We could take it from you right now.
narrate Hercule: W-w-wait! Take this instead! A real Dragon Ball! My trophy from the last tournament! It's worth a fortune!
narrate He drops it in the dirt and runs behind a car. The ball is grey and heavy. Two stars, carved in stone.
say android17 It's a rock.
say android18 Keep it. It's funny.
do call 129 16 1
set_flag 411
journal Stone Dragon Balls: some old fool says there were seven of them.
stop
label herc_after
narrate Hercule (from behind the car): I've got a little girl at home! Videl! She's fifteen! Please go away!
stop

# ---------- Kami's Lookout (17:43, BF 6:1)
list lookout_arrive
if_flag 412 lookout_seen
set_flag 412
narrate Kami's Lookout. The garden has gone to seed. Weeds push up between the white tiles.
narrate Nobody tends it any more. The god who lived here died the day the androids killed Piccolo.
say android18 There's nobody here.
say android17 Good. Then nobody can tell us to leave.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label lookout_seen
list lookout_door
if_flag 413 altar_done
if_flag 411 a1
goto altar_lore
label a1
if_flag 415 a2
goto altar_lore
label a2
if_flag 418 a3
goto altar_lore
label a3
if_flag 421 a4
goto altar_lore
label a4
if_flag 426 a5
goto altar_lore
label a5
if_flag 427 a6
goto altar_lore
label a6
if_flag 428 altar_all
goto altar_lore
label altar_lore
narrate The palace doors stand open. Inside, an empty throne and a carved stone altar with seven hollows in it.
narrate Seven hollows, each the size of a ball.
stop
label altar_all
narrate Eighteen sets the seven stone balls in the seven hollows, one at a time.
narrate Nothing happens. No light. No dragon. Just seven grey rocks in a row.
say android18 ...I thought something would happen.
say android17 You wanted to make a wish?
say android18 Maybe.
say android17 For what?
say android18 I don't know. Something that isn't this.
narrate Behind the altar, a cupboard the gods kept stocked: holy water, and a jar of beans.
do call 129 10 2; call 129 11 3; call 129 9 1
set_flag 413
journal The Dragon Balls are stone. There are no wishes left.
stop
label altar_done
narrate Seven grey stones in seven hollows. The wind moves the curtains. Nothing else moves.
stop

# ---------- Papaya Island (17:44, BF 7:1: the tournament gate)
list papaya_arrive
if_flag 414 papaya_seen
set_flag 414
narrate Papaya Island. The World Martial Arts Tournament was held here every few years. The banners are rags now.
narrate A few fighters still train in the plaza, waiting for a tournament that isn't coming.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label papaya_seen
list papaya_gate
narrate The gate to the tournament grounds is welded shut. A hand-painted sign: NO TOURNAMENT THIS YEAR. Under it, older paint: OR NEXT YEAR.
stop
list papaya_announcer
if_flag 415 ann_after
narrate Announcer: Well! It's been a long time since anyone famous came to Papaya Island!
narrate Announcer: I called the last great tournament, you know. Goku against the demon king! What a match!
say android18 Goku. The one who died before we woke up.
narrate Announcer: A heart virus, of all things. The strongest man in the world. Life's not fair, is it?
narrate Announcer: I kept the grand prize for the next champion. It went to stone years ago, but... here. You two are the only fighters left.
narrate A grey stone ball with seven stars.
do call 129 21 1
set_flag 415
stop
label ann_after
narrate Announcer: If anyone ever holds a tournament again, I'll be right here. Somebody has to say the names.
stop

# ---------- Diablo Desert (17:45, BF 14:1: Prototype 11)
list diablo_arrive
if_flag 416 diablo_seen
set_flag 416
narrate Diablo Desert. A bandit called Yamcha used to rob travellers here, before he ever met Goku.
narrate Something big is standing in the dead trees. Red Ribbon paint, twenty years faded.
say android17 One of the old man's toys. It's still running.
say android18 It's guarding something.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label diablo_seen
list diablo_ball
if_flag 418 dball_done
if_flag 417 dball_take
narrate Prototype 11 stands over the spot. Its last order came from a general who has been dead for twenty years: GUARD THE DRAGON BALL.
stop
label dball_take
narrate Under the wreck of Prototype 11, a Red Ribbon field case. Inside: a Dragon Ball radar, dead, and a grey stone ball with three stars.
say android17 The Red Ribbon Army went looking for these when the old man was still working for them.
say android18 And they found one. And then Goku tore the army apart, and nobody came back for it.
do call 129 17 1
set_flag 418
stop
label dball_done
narrate An empty Red Ribbon field case, half buried in sand.
stop

# ---------- Pilaf's Castle (17:46, BF 13:1)
list pilaf_arrive
if_flag 419 pilaf_seen
set_flag 419
narrate The ruins of a castle in the jungle. A tattered flag still flies over the rubble: a little blue emperor's crest.
narrate Ninjas move between the trees. Somebody is still guarding whatever is left.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label pilaf_seen
list pilaf_safe
if_flag 421 psafe_done
if_flag 420 psafe_open
narrate A collapsed treasure room. A heavy safe sits in the rubble. The ninjas keep watching it.
stop
label psafe_open
narrate With their captain beaten, the ninjas are gone. The safe door hangs open: a ledger of schemes, a map of the world, and a grey ball with six stars.
narrate The ledger's last page: WORLD DOMINATION, STEP 1: COLLECT THE DRAGON BALLS. It's crossed out. Under it: STEP 1: SURVIVE.
do call 129 20 1
set_flag 421
stop
label psafe_done
narrate An empty safe and a ledger nobody will finish.
stop

# ---------- Nataday Village (17:47, BF 15:1)
list nat_arrive
if_flag 422 nat_seen
set_flag 422
narrate Nataday Village. A few farms that the androids never bothered to burn.
narrate Someone else has found them instead. Raiders, picking the village clean.
say android17 Look at that. Little thieves, working our territory.
say android18 Don't pretend you care about these people.
say android17 I don't. I care about the principle.
journal Run the raiders out of Nataday Village
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label nat_seen
list nat_elder
if_flag 426 elder_after
if_flag 423 elder_give
narrate Elder: Please. We have nothing left. Take what you want and go.
narrate Elder: ...You're not with Butcher's gang? Then you'd better hide. He takes everything that isn't nailed down.
stop
label elder_give
narrate Elder: Butcher's gone. His boys are running. I don't know why you did it, and I won't ask.
narrate Elder: My husband found this in the river when we were young. It was pretty then. It's only stone now. Take it.
narrate A grey stone ball with five stars.
do call 129 19 1; call 129 11 1
set_flag 426
stop
label elder_after
narrate Elder: The children have started playing outside again. Don't take that away from them.
stop
list nat_farmer
narrate Farmer: Butcher and his boys came down from the hills last month. Took the seed corn, the radio, my good boots.
stop

# ---------- the stone balls in the chapter 9 places
list paozu_ball
if_flag 427 pball_done
narrate On a cushion by the window, a small shrine: a photograph of an old man with a staff, and a grey stone ball with four stars.
say android18 It's his grandfather's. Gohan's great-grandfather. She keeps it dusted.
say android17 Take it. She's got the photo.
narrate Eighteen hesitates. Then she takes it.
do call 129 18 1
set_flag 427
stop
label pball_done
narrate The cushion where the stone ball used to sit. The photograph is still there.
stop
list kame_ball
if_flag 428 kball_done
narrate In the wreck of Kame House, under a pile of magazines nobody will read again: a grey stone ball with one star.
do call 129 15 1
set_flag 428
stop
label kball_done
narrate Pink boards and a lot of sand.
stop
